00:37:46.780 --> 00:37:52.798
His birthday is April 30th, so he was born on April 30th of 2007, and so that would have been, yeah, right?
他的生日是 4 月 30 日，所以他出生于 2007 年 4 月 30 日，所以，是的，对吧？

00:37:52.798 --> 00:37:57.579
And I think we would have been on hiatus for over a month or something at that point.
我认为那时我们会中断一个多月或其他时间。

00:37:57.579 --> 00:38:02.968
And it was like, oh, perfect timing, hiatus, baby, he'll be born, it'll be the, well, I'll have the baby.
就好像，哦，完美的时机，中断，宝贝，他会出生，那就是，好吧，我会生下孩子。

00:38:02.968 --> 00:38:05.739
I was really going to be the first in my friend group.
我真的想成为我的朋友组中的第一个。

00:38:05.739 --> 00:38:12.059
One of them, Alec was, Alec, our producer was also having a baby in that same hiatus.
其中之一，亚历克，我们的制片人亚历克也在同一时期生了孩子。

00:38:12.059 --> 00:38:18.780
But we were young, not everyone had kids on the show, the cast, we were like, ah, we're going first.
但我们还年轻，不是每个人都有孩子参加演出，演员们，我们就像，啊，我们先走。

00:38:18.780 --> 00:38:19.780
And it would be great.
那就太好了。

00:38:19.780 --> 00:38:27.940
The baby will come out, it will be a nice couple months with the baby and then back to work, easy, peasy, and then life will all make sense and have a perfect shape after that.
宝宝会出生，和宝宝一起度过美好的几个月，然后回到工作岗位，轻松、轻松，然后生活就会变得有意义，并拥有一个完美的形状。

00:38:27.940 --> 00:38:29.340
That's not what happened.
事实并非如此。

00:38:29.340 --> 00:38:38.051
What happened is that Elliot was born and we had no idea until he was born that he needed open heart surgery, he weighed much less than anticipated.
埃利奥特出生了，直到他出生我们才知道他需要进行心脏直视手术，他的体重比预期的要轻得多。

00:38:38.051 --> 00:38:45.350
No wonder what it was for the first week, the thought was he has viral pneumonia, he has this, he has that it was all wrong.
难怪第一周会发生什么，我的想法是他得了病毒性肺炎，他有这个，他有这一切都是错误的。

00:38:45.350 --> 00:38:58.299
We had a bunch of misdiagnoses at one hospital, we moved to this hospital children's hospital of Los Angeles, which was amazing and saved my son's life, diagnosed him correctly and saved his life with open heart surgery.
我们在一家医院发生了一系列误诊，我们搬到了这家医院的洛杉矶儿童医院，这真是太棒了，挽救了我儿子的生命，正确诊断了他，并通过心脏直视手术挽救了他的生命。

00:38:58.299 --> 00:39:09.247
And what he had was something called Jacobson syndrome, which is a genetic syndrome where, for no reason at all, just a random chance, it's called the de novo deletion, a lightning bolt.
他得的是雅各布森综合症，这是一种遗传综合症，没有任何原因，只是一个随机的机会，这被称为从头删除，闪电。

00:39:09.247 --> 00:39:17.900
A little piece of the 11th chromosome is missing, which means there are a bunch of health ramifications and a bunch of developmental ramifications.
第 11 号染色体缺失一小部分，这意味着会产生一系列健康影响和一系列发育影响。

00:39:18.940 --> 00:39:19.633
So he was born.
于是他就诞生了。

00:39:19.633 --> 00:39:21.530
We were called down to the bad news room.
我们被叫到坏消息室。

00:39:21.530 --> 00:39:28.054
We had been in the neonatal intensive care unit with this kid who weighed three and a half pounds, who were told he needs open heart surgery.
我们和这个重三磅半的孩子一起住在新生儿重症监护室，他被告知需要进行心脏直视手术。

00:39:28.054 --> 00:39:30.459
That's what he was born at, three and a half pounds.
这就是他出生时的体重，三磅半。

00:39:30.460 --> 00:39:33.460
It was like three pounds, 10 out of 11 ounces, something like that.
就像 3 磅，11 盎司中的 10 盎司，类似的东西。

00:39:33.460 --> 00:39:36.460
And they couldn't tell that from like the scan.
他们无法从扫描中看出这一点。

00:39:36.460 --> 00:39:38.820
They thought he was small, my wife is five feet tall.
他们认为他很小，我的妻子有五英尺高。

00:39:38.820 --> 00:39:41.500
They were like, she was a small baby, but they were off.
他们就像，她是一个小婴儿，但他们离开了。

00:39:41.500 --> 00:39:43.460
The estimation, it's so funny.
这个估计，太搞笑了。

00:39:43.460 --> 00:39:44.780
2007 is long enough.
2007年已经够长了。

00:39:44.780 --> 00:39:47.179
I got that like technology has gotten much better.
我明白技术已经变得更好了。

00:39:47.179 --> 00:39:48.980
The scans would have shown more.
扫描会显示更多。

00:39:48.980 --> 00:39:50.619
Things would have been more accurate.
事情本来会更准确。

00:39:50.619 --> 00:39:53.340
They thought he was always a little small, but I guess it makes sense.
他们认为他总是有点小，但我想这是有道理的。

00:39:53.340 --> 00:39:57.820
The mom's small, but it turned out to be smaller than they thought.
妈妈很小，但事实证明比他们想象的要小。

00:39:57.820 --> 00:40:04.444
And he had the open heart surgery, and all the doctors thought was he was born with these random heart problems.
他接受了心脏直视手术，所有医生都认为他天生患有这些随机的心脏问题。

00:40:04.444 --> 00:40:05.450
No one knows why.
没有人知道为什么。

00:40:05.450 --> 00:40:15.564
And only after the successful life-saving open heart surgery where they were operating on this tiny heart with the description wasn't so vivid and vivid and unforgettable.
而只有在成功救生的心脏直视手术之后，他们在这颗小小的心脏上进行手术时，描述才不再那么生动、生动和难忘。

00:40:15.564 --> 00:40:20.059
And this is not what you want to be thinking about when you're a new parent.
当您成为新父母时，这不是您想要考虑的问题。

00:40:20.059 --> 00:40:24.219
They said, we'll be operating on veins the size of dental floss.
他们说，我们将在牙线大小的静脉上进行手术。

00:40:24.219 --> 00:40:25.059
Oh, my God.
我的天啊。

00:40:25.059 --> 00:40:34.460
And you say, oh, and they tell you all the percentages of ways it could go wrong, and it adds up to like, this is a 50-50 search, but the outcome's 50-50.
你说，哦，他们会告诉你可能出错的所有百分比，加起来就像，这是一个 50-50 的搜索，但结果是 50-50。

00:40:34.460 --> 00:40:37.659
Toss a coin of whether he will live.
抛硬币决定他是否能活下去。

00:40:37.659 --> 00:40:46.300
And we, it was a successful open heart surgery to fixing four things, two holes in the wall of his heart.
我们进行了一次成功的心脏直视手术，修复了四个东西，即他心壁上的两个洞。

00:40:46.300 --> 00:40:51.099
This extra piece called a core triadriatum, which is just this deformed part that had to be fixed.
这个额外的部分称为核心三体，这正是必须修复的变形部分。

00:40:51.099 --> 00:40:53.980
But not one of the, that's the least of the problems.
但这不是其中之一，这是最不重要的问题。

00:40:53.980 --> 00:40:56.579
and the two holes are closeable on ASD and a VSD.
ASD 和 VSD 上的两个孔是可以关闭的。

00:40:56.579 --> 00:41:11.420
And then this much bigger problem called total anomalous pulmonary venous return TAPVR that is the really wrongly wired veins that went instead of coming from the heart back to the lungs went down to the liver.
然后，这个更大的问题被称为完全肺静脉回流异常（TAPVR），即真正错误连接的静脉，不是从心脏返回肺部，而是向下到达肝脏。

00:41:11.420 --> 00:41:24.639
And did this incredible, what in retrospect was this incredible improvisation in order, what was really going on is the genetic map to properly form a heart was off because of the missing piece of that chromosome.
这令人难以置信，回想起来，这是令人难以置信的即兴创作，真正发生的是正确形成心脏的基因图谱由于缺失了该染色体的一部分而被关闭。

00:41:24.639 --> 00:41:43.679
But Elliot, improvisational musician that he is today at age 19, his heart improvised a route and the veins were sent somewhere else and like MacGyverd their way back throw through the liver into his heart to exist in utero.
但是埃利奥特，一位即兴音乐家，如今已经 19 岁了，他的心脏临时搭建了一条路线，静脉被送往其他地方，就像麦盖佛德一样，通过肝脏回到他的心脏，在子宫内存在。

00:41:43.679 --> 00:41:47.800
But once you are born, you cannot get enough oxygen that way.
但一旦你出生，你就无法通过这种方式获得足够的氧气。

00:41:47.800 --> 00:41:49.880
And that's why his oxygen was so low.
这就是他的氧气含量如此低的原因。

00:41:49.880 --> 00:41:51.960
but no one knew why.
但没有人知道为什么。

00:41:51.960 --> 00:42:02.159
And they had to fix all of these four heart problems in a half hour by stopping his heart and pumping his blood through a machine.
他们必须在半小时内通过停止心脏跳动并通过机器泵血来解决所有这四种心脏问题。

00:42:02.159 --> 00:42:06.519
And if it's any longer than a half hour, it's the disaster.
如果超过半小时，那就是灾难了。

00:42:06.519 --> 00:42:17.519
So this amazing doctor, Dr. von Starns at Children's Hospital of Los Angeles, who many years later is the doctor who did the open heart surgery on Jimmy Kimmel's son.
这位了不起的医生，洛杉矶儿童医院的冯·斯塔恩斯医生，多年后为吉米·金梅尔的儿子做了心脏直视手术。

00:42:17.519 --> 00:42:24.199
And also, and this is, he's usually a specialist, people fly from all over the world to see this doctor, Dr. Starnes.
而且，他通常是一位专家，人们从世界各地飞来见这位医生，斯塔恩斯医生。

00:42:24.199 --> 00:42:32.559
Usually he does only kids, or mainly kids, but he also operated on Arnold Schwarzenegger and did a quintuple bypass, I think.
通常他只给孩子做手术，或者主要是孩子，但我认为他也给阿诺·施瓦辛格做了手术，并且做了五次搭桥手术。

00:42:32.559 --> 00:42:38.579
So I'd like to say Elliot and the Terminator's heart had the same dude's hands on it on them.
所以我想说艾略特和终结者的心都被同一个家伙所触动了。

00:42:39.480 --> 00:42:40.880
And Jimmy Kimmel's son.
还有吉米·金梅尔的儿子。

00:42:40.880 --> 00:42:43.880
So we all have a weird little bond.
所以我们都有一种奇怪的小联系。

00:42:43.880 --> 00:42:50.960
isn't it weird that in one summer, you became like a pretty quick cardiac expert.
在一个夏天里，你变得像一位速度很快的心脏病专家，这不是很奇怪吗？

00:42:50.960 --> 00:42:53.440
Like you still know these terms today.
就像您今天仍然知道这些术语一样。

00:42:53.440 --> 00:42:55.239
Oh yeah, my wife is the genius.
哦，是的，我的妻子是个天才。

00:42:55.239 --> 00:43:02.480
My wife has retained all of this and still does and there's still things we have to know about the heart and she is the genius library about.
我的妻子保留了所有这些，现在仍然保留，还有一些关于心脏的事情我们必须了解，她是天才图书馆。

00:43:02.480 --> 00:43:08.519
She discovered this facility and for this language and I'm okay at it, but she's amazing at it.
她发现了这种设施和这种语言，我很擅长，但她很擅长。

00:43:08.519 --> 00:43:14.239
She had to just become an expert because Jacobson syndrome is very, very rare.
她必须成为一名专家，因为雅各布森综合症非常非常罕见。

00:43:14.239 --> 00:43:25.079
So we wound up, my hiatus between season two and three was six and a half weeks in the neonatal intensive care unit with my son in a plastic box.
所以我们结束了，第二季和第三季之间我的休息时间是六周半，我和我的儿子在一个塑料盒子里，在新生儿重症监护室里。

00:43:25.079 --> 00:43:28.599
And it was so strange.
这太奇怪了。

00:43:28.599 --> 00:43:33.119
Our lives just felt like they had gone to in a completely different direction than anticipated.
我们的生活感觉已经走向了与预期完全不同的方向。

00:43:33.119 --> 00:43:39.119
And in the back of my head is each day ticked away, I thought I would have to think, I've got a launch season three of this TV show.
在我的脑海里，每一天都在流逝，我想我必须想，我已经推出了这个电视节目的第三季。

00:43:39.119 --> 00:43:39.960
Pretty soon.
很快。

00:43:39.960 --> 00:43:40.800
Now go be funny.
现在去搞笑吧。

00:43:40.800 --> 00:43:41.300
be funny.
有趣一点。

00:43:41.300 --> 00:43:42.537
That's what I would say.
我就是这么说的。

00:43:42.537 --> 00:43:47.024
I would go into the rants and to run running the show in the beginning of season three.
我会在第三季开始时大声咆哮并主持节目。

00:43:47.024 --> 00:43:52.800
And I would plop down the couch in my office with Carter and we'd look into each other and say, now go be funny.
我会和卡特一起坐在办公室的沙发上，我们互相看着对方说，现在去搞笑吧。

00:43:52.800 --> 00:43:57.339
It was like I was living in this intense medical drama and then commuting into a sitcom.
就好像我生活在这部激烈的医疗剧中，然后又进入了一部情景喜剧。

00:43:57.339 --> 00:43:59.195
It was just such a bizarre whiplash.
这真是一次奇怪的鞭打。

00:43:59.159 --> 00:44:01.771
Can I ask you a couple more questions?
我可以再问你几个问题吗？

00:44:01.771 --> 00:44:03.971
How long was he in the hospital?
他在医院住了多久？

00:44:03.971 --> 00:44:05.552
It was about six weeks.
大约有六个星期。

00:44:05.552 --> 00:44:08.301
So were you guys living at the hospital?
那么你们住在医院吗？

00:44:08.301 --> 00:44:08.920
Were you?
你是吗？

00:44:08.920 --> 00:44:30.039
We had one point where I think staying in a hotel room at a hospital, but we didn't live that far from it, so we eventually were spending a bunch of time right at the hospital and almost never leaving and just going to a hotel to crash for a few hours and going to the hospital, but eventually we realized we were dying inside and we needed to start going home and shifting it out a little bit.
有一次，我想我们住在医院的酒店房间里，但我们住的地方离医院不远，所以我们最终在医院里呆了很多时间，几乎从来没有离开过，只是去一家酒店住了几个小时，然后去了医院，但最终我们意识到我们快要死在里面了，我们需要开始回家，把它移出去一点。

00:44:30.039 --> 00:44:31.639
Were you guys able to hold him?
你们能抱住他吗？

00:44:31.639 --> 00:44:32.639
No.
不。

00:44:32.639 --> 00:44:43.142
We were mostly not able to hold him for a while, so after that surgery he was hooked up to so many tubes, he had this, you know, gnarly scar down his chest held together by staples and metal and stitches.
我们基本上无法让他保持一段时间，所以手术后他被连接了很多管子，他的胸部有一个粗糙的疤痕，用订书钉、金属和缝线固定在一起。

00:44:43.142 --> 00:45:01.624
At one point, the gnarliest moment was, and I'll just talk about this because who, maybe someone out there needs to hear this, maybe someone's been through this, maybe someone will hear this and later go through this, but they can't close up the chest due to swelling after an open heart surgery when the baby weighs three pounds, so they had to tape it shut.
在某一时刻，最棘手的时刻是，我只想谈谈这个，因为谁，也许外面有人需要听到这个，也许有人经历过这个，也许有人会听到这个，然后再经历这个，但是由于心脏直视手术后婴儿重三磅，肿胀，他们无法关闭胸部，所以他们不得不用胶带将其关闭。

00:45:01.624 --> 00:45:04.301
So you could see the heart beating through the tape.
所以你可以通过录像带看到心脏的跳动。

00:45:04.301 --> 00:45:07.802
And my wife made the terrible mistake, tough, tough guy that she is.
我的妻子犯了一个可怕的错误，她是个坚强的人。

00:45:07.802 --> 00:45:10.273
She's like, I'm going to go take a look at that.
她说，我要去看看。

00:45:10.273 --> 00:45:12.178
They really recommended not doing it.
他们真的建议不要这样做。

00:45:12.178 --> 00:45:14.391
Like, we're going to leave this covered up.
就像，我们要把这件事掩盖起来。

00:45:14.391 --> 00:45:16.862
It's only going to be this way for a day or two.
这种情况只会持续一两天。

00:45:16.862 --> 00:45:21.187
My wife is like, she's like this dancer, choreographer, kinesiologist, anatomy nerd.
我的妻子就像这个舞者、编舞家、运动学家、解剖学呆子。

00:45:21.187 --> 00:45:23.040
She's like, I think I can handle it.
她说，我想我能应付。

00:45:23.040 --> 00:45:24.430
I'm going to go look at it.
我要去看看。

00:45:24.430 --> 00:45:25.769
She went and looked at it.
她走过去看了看。

00:45:25.769 --> 00:45:27.880
She was like, bring that chair over here.
她说，把椅子搬过来。

00:45:27.880 --> 00:45:31.154
I think I'm going to pass out and split a chair on her and she didn't.
我想我会昏倒并把一把椅子劈在她身上，但她没有。

00:45:31.154 --> 00:45:33.400
She didn't, but that she couldn't stand anymore.
她没有，但她已经无法忍受了。

00:45:33.400 --> 00:45:37.559
And so that, it was just the most visceral experience.
所以，这只是最发自内心的体验。

00:45:37.559 --> 00:45:43.360
And then of course, the geneticist calls you down, we celebrated that he lived through this open hearts injury.
当然，遗传学家叫你下来，我们庆祝他经历了这种开放的心灵伤害。

00:45:43.360 --> 00:45:47.000
And then the genetic, we get this message, the geneticist wants to see you now.
然后是遗传学，我们得到这个消息，遗传学家现在想见你。

00:45:47.000 --> 00:45:48.280
And we're like, okay, yeah, send her in here.
我们就像，好吧，是的，把她送到这里。

00:45:48.280 --> 00:45:49.760
Here we are at the Isolette.
我们来到了伊索莱特酒店。

00:45:49.760 --> 00:45:53.119
The word for those plastic boxes is called an Isolette.
这些塑料盒被称为“Isolette”。

00:45:53.119 --> 00:45:55.679
Isolette is the perfect fucking word.
Isolette 是一个完美的词。

00:45:55.679 --> 00:46:07.639
Isolette, it sounds like some haunted fairy tale world, isolate, and you feel very alone when you're in and around the isolate, and we get called.
伊索莱特，这听起来像是一些闹鬼的童话世界，隔离，当你在隔离中或周围时，你会感到非常孤独，我们就会接到电话。

00:46:07.639 --> 00:46:09.517
We were like, oh, send her in here.
我们就像，哦，把她送来这里。

00:46:09.517 --> 00:46:10.429
We live here now.
我们现在住在这里。

00:46:10.429 --> 00:46:12.199
We live next to this plastic box.
我们住在这个塑料盒子旁边。

00:46:12.199 --> 00:46:12.746
No, no.
不，不。

00:46:12.746 --> 00:46:17.198
The geneticist has booked a private room to speak to you.
遗传学家已经预订了一个私人房间来与您交谈。

00:46:17.198 --> 00:46:35.319
I'm like, that doesn't seem good, and you do that long walk down this hallway, you find the room, you open the door, it's a windowless room, couch, couple chairs, Kleenex, just the box of tissues, and like, this is the bad newsroom.
我想，这看起来不太好，你沿着走廊走了很长一段路，找到房间，打开门，这是一个没有窗户的房间，沙发，几把椅子，面巾纸，只有一盒纸巾，就像，这是坏新闻编辑室。

00:46:35.320 --> 00:46:40.072
And that was the room where we were told that this isn't just hard problems.
正是在这个房间里，我们被告知这不仅仅是难题。

00:46:40.072 --> 00:46:41.761
This is a genetic syndrome.
这是一种遗传综合症。

00:46:41.761 --> 00:46:43.575
He'll have it his whole life.
他一生都会拥有它。

00:46:43.575 --> 00:46:55.957
The geneticist who had never seen an actual kid in her career with Jacobson syndrome, because it's that rare, basically had the Google print out of like everything associated with Jacobson syndrome.
